'''Toxoglossa''' (tok-sō-glos′ä), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < Gr. τοξικόν, poison, + γλῶσσα, a tongue.] An order or suborder of pectinibranchiate gastropods.
{{smaller block|They have two (rarely four) rows of marginal teeth, which are generally perforated and penetrated by a secretion from a veneniferous gland, and there are rarely median teeth. The division includes the families ''Conidæ'', ''Pleurotomidæ'', and ''Terebridæ'', and related forms. Also ''Toxiglossa'', ''Toxifera''. See cuts under ''Conus'', ''Pleurotoma'', and ''Terebra''.}}

